cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NablaEngine: fast and exact differentiable physics simulation for embodied AI"
abstract: >-
  A differentiable GPU physics engine, built first for the Unitree G1 humanoid (mjlab model) and since 1.0.0 for a
  wider class of MuJoCo models (several kinematic trees, motors, meshes, equality constraints, tendons). It runs a whole control step
  (collision, constraints, Newton solver and implicitfast integration over several substeps) for thousands of worlds
  in one call, one warp per world in fused CUDA kernels, and provides an analytic adjoint of that step with JAX and
  PyTorch interfaces. The engine is checked against MuJoCo and MuJoCo Warp.
authors:
  - name: "The NablaEngine Authors"
version: 1.0.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/sailab-ai/NablaEngine"
keywords:
  - physics simulation
  - differentiable simulation
  - CUDA
  - JAX
  - MuJoCo
  - robotics
  - humanoid
